# macOS

The current CI workflow builds and tests on `macos-latest` using Homebrew
dependencies and disables SCTP. This does not verify the Homebrew
`freediameter` formula or older macOS releases.

Install Xcode Command Line Tools and Homebrew using their current official
instructions, then install CMake, Bison, GnuTLS, libgcrypt, and libidn2 with
Homebrew. Homebrew's Bison may not be on the default PATH; use its explicit
path when configuring:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/freeDiameter/freeDiameter.git
cd freeDiameter
mkdir test.build
cd test.build
cmake .. \
  -DDISABLE_SCTP=ON \
  -DBISON_EXECUTABLE="$(brew --prefix bison)/bin/bison"
cmake --build .
ctest --output-on-failure
```

SCTP is disabled in this configuration because the current macOS CI job does
not validate it. See `INSTALL` for general build requirements and test notes.
